WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.500
Target-based CMake is more than a modern style preference.

2
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:09.880
It is a way to express build intent at the level where the intent actually applies.

3
00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:22.220
Libraries, executables, tests, tools, and generated components can each carry their own include paths, compile definitions, compile options, link dependencies, and language requirements.

4
00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:26.560
This makes the project easier to reason about and easier to review.

5
00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:31.000
Public, private, and interface properties are especially important.

6
00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:36.300
A private include path should help one target compile without leaking into downstream users.

7
00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:39.600
A public dependency becomes part of the contract for consumers.

8
00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:44.420
An interface property can carry requirements without building a binary of its own.

9
00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:51.480
When those scopes are chosen deliberately, the CMake files describe both implementation detail and integration boundary.

10
00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:54.560
Broad global settings create hidden coupling.

11
00:00:54.660 --> 00:01:01.620
A global include directory can make an unrelated target compile only because it accidentally sees headers it should not depend on.

12
00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:07.880
A global compile definition can change behavior across the project with little visibility.

13
00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:15.340
A global linker option may apply to tools, tests, and production binaries even when only one target needed it.

14
00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:20.340
A secure project structure helps reviewers see where trust boundaries exist.

15
00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:31.240
Internal libraries, third-party dependencies, command-line tools, plugins, and shipped executables should be named and organized so their relationships are visible.

16
00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:41.340
The closer CMake stays to the architecture of the software, the easier it becomes to identify unnecessary exposure, surprising inheritance, and changes that deserve deeper review before release.
